Pre-existing backend defect found during NEARS-2451 regression sweep (unrelated
to this ticket's Flutter-only diff; filed as regression_bug, not a task_bug).

GET /api/v1/items/most-reviewed ignores the `search` query param entirely --
total_size is identical across every search term, while the sibling
GET /api/v1/items/popular endpoint correctly filters on the same param.

Live curl evidence (zone 1, Food module, via QA fault-proxy pass-through on
port 26933 -> real backend 127.0.0.1:8000):

  most-reviewed search='':       total_size=30
  most-reviewed search='ch':     total_size=30   (expected < 30, unchanged)
  most-reviewed search='qwxzj':  total_size=30   (expected 0, nonsense term)
  most-reviewed search='Burger': total_size=30   (expected < 30, unchanged)

  popular search='':       total_size=85
  popular search='ch':     total_size=22   (correctly filtered)
  popular search='qwxzj':  total_size=0    (correctly filtered)

Root cause (read, not modified):
  Admin/app/Http/Controllers/Api/V1/ItemController.php
    get_popular_products() line 528:
      ProductLogic::popular_products($zone_id, ..., $rating_count, $request['search']);
        -- passes $request['search'] through.
    get_most_reviewed_products() lines 533-552:
      never reads $request->query('search') at all, and calls
      ProductLogic::most_reviewed_products($zone_id, ..., $rating_count) with NO
      search argument -- the param is silently dropped server-side.
    Contrast: get_discounted_products() (line 554+, deleted axis per NEARS-2181
    but still present as dead code) DOES pass search:$request['search']??null,
    so the omission on most_reviewed is specific to that one handler, not a
    systemic pattern.

Impact on THIS ticket: none on the ACs demonstrated (the first-page-failure /
NErrorRetry / retry mechanism is fetch-agnostic to whether the backend response
data reflects the search term -- a 500 status still triggers the correct client
behaviour regardless). Confirmed zero overlap with files changed by NEARS-2451
(UserApp/lib/features/item/controllers/item_controller.dart,
UserApp/lib/features/item/screens/item_view_all_screen.dart) -- this is a
backend-only (Admin/) defect the Flutter diff cannot have introduced.
